      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 911: 🔴 `pw_ctx-\u003eframe_size \u003d pw_ctx-\u003ewidth * pw_ctx-\u003eheight * pw_ctx-\u003eBpp;` performs arithmetic on 32-bit operands before assignment, so very large negotiated dimensions can overflow before the later size check. The same pattern appears in DMA size computation (`offset + pitch * height`). Use checked/widened arithmetic (`size_t` casts before multiply/add plus overflow guards, or FFmpeg size helpers) and reject invalid dimensions early to prevent undersized allocations/metadata and potential memory-safety issues.",
      "revId": "4bb310340791bca59c6af870b17b3e550d62eebc",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
