      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 1276: 🔴 `memcpy(..., row_size)` uses negotiated width while source stride comes from PipeWire metadata, but there is no validation that `chunk-\u003estride` is positive and at least `row_size`, nor that `offset + stride * (height-1) + row_size` stays within the mapped buffer. A malformed/buggy producer can trigger out-of-bounds reads. Add explicit bounds checks before copying and drop/recycle the frame on invalid geometry.",
      "revId": "4bb310340791bca59c6af870b17b3e550d62eebc",
